                  "kind": "text",
                  "data": "You're asking how to run the build/deploy when:\n\n1. The source is on the router (at `/srv/git/odbus`)\n2. Your laptop doesn't have the source\n3. The router isn't reachable from your VPS\n\nYour options:\n\n**Option A: Build directly on the router**\n\nSSH into the router and run:\n\n```bash\ncd /srv/git/odbus\nCXXFLAGS=\"-include cstdint\" cargo build --workspace --release\nsudo deploy/runit/build-golden.sh\n```\n\nThis is the intended path — the deploy script publishes locally.\n\n**Option B: If you can't SSH to the router right now**\n\nYou're stuck. The build must happen where the source lives (or where a btrfs subvolume can be snapshotted). The deployment model is btrfs send/receive, not copying binaries over the network.\n\n**What would fix this long-term:**\n\n- Push the repo to a remote (GitHub/Gitea/bare repo on VPS) so you can clone it anywhere\n- Set up a WireGuard tunnel from VPS to router so you always have access\n- Or run a git mirror on the VPS that syncs from the router when it's reachable\n\nWhich of these is your situation — can you SSH to the router from your laptop directly, or are you completely locked out right now?"
